{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:QOU.KnotRegistry","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.YekutieliTriple","lean:module:QOU.ArchimedeanMassFormula","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Real.Irrational","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.PSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed"],"declarations":54,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerNoncollapseImpliesIndependence.independence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerNoncollapseImpliesIndependence.independence","kind":"theorem","line":705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L705-L705","doc":"The independence witness produced by the bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerNoncollapseImpliesIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerNoncollapseImpliesIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":702,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L702-L702","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerNoncollapseImpliesIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerNoncollapseImpliesIndependence","kind":"class","line":696,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L696-L705","doc":"**Tower-noncollapse → independence — typeclass.**\n\nConjectural Nesterenko-type bridge: any Yekutieli lifting\ncondition implies algebraic independence of hyperbolic volumes.\nBound to a specific Yekutieli witness so the conjectural\ncontent is visible at the call site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.implies_borel_zagier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.implies_borel_zagier","kind":"theorem","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L606-L675","doc":"Algebraic independence implies ℚ-linear independence.\n\nDIAGNOSTIC: the witness construction uses a 3-element `Finset`\nexpansion `{(1,0,0), (0,1,0), (0,0,1)}` together with an\nindicator `f` whose support equals `S`.  The two intermediate\nobligations — `hf_supp` (`f` vanishes off `S`) and `hf_sum`\n(the weighted sum equals zero) — both require carefully\nmatched `simp` rewrites against current Mathlib (`Ne.def`,\n`decide_True`, `Prod.mk.injEq` lemma names have churned\nrepeatedly).  Closing them robustly requires either:\n1. switching to `Fin 3 → ℚ` and `Fin.sum_univ_three`, which\n   avoids `Finset.insert` decidability; or\n2. defining `S` as `Finset.image` of `Fin 3` to give a clean\n   cardinality-3 witness.\nSorry retained pending refactor to a Fin-indexed witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.implies_single_irrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.implies_single_irrational","kind":"theorem","line":497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L497-L604","doc":"**Algebraic independence implies irrationality of each volume.**\n\nThe proof is a 2-monomial contradiction: if `vol_v = (r : ℝ)` for some\n`r : ℚ`, then the polynomial `P(v) = v − r` (support `{(1,0,0),(0,0,0)}`\nresp. the appropriate unit index) gives a nontrivial zero polynomial\nrelation, contradicting `HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.no_relation`.\n\nNote: `BorelZagierQOU` alone is insufficient for this implication.\nℚ-linear independence of {vol_4_1, vol_5_2, vol_B3} does not exclude the\npossibility that some volume equals a rational (counterexample: {1, π, e}\nis ℚ-linearly independent yet 1 ∈ ℚ).  Algebraic independence is needed,\nand is the correct hypothesis here.\n\nRef: [zagier1986] https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0084581 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelZagierQOU.linear_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelZagierQOU.linear_independent","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L492-L492","doc":"No rational linear combination vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelZagierQOU.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelZagierQOU.mk","kind":"ctor","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L489-L489","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelZagierQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelZagierQOU","kind":"class","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L484-L495","doc":"**Conjecture (Borel–Zagier for QOU volumes).**\nThe three volumes are ℚ-linearly independent: no non-trivial\nrational linear combination vanishes.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:borel-zagier-qou-volumes}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.vol_B3_irrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.vol_B3_irrational","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L482-L482","doc":"Vol(𝓑₃) ∉ ℚ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.vol_5_2_irrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.vol_5_2_irrational","kind":"theorem","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L480-L480","doc":"Vol(5₂) ∉ ℚ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.vol_4_1_irrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.vol_4_1_irrational","kind":"theorem","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L477-L477","doc":"Vol(4₁) ∉ ℚ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational.mk","kind":"ctor","line":475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L475-L475","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational","kind":"class","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L471-L482","doc":"**Conjecture (Irrationality of a single volume).**\nVol(4₁) = 2 Cl₂(π/3) = 6 Λ(π/3) is irrational.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:single-volume-irrationality}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.no_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.no_relation","kind":"theorem","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L459-L459","doc":"No non-trivial monomial relation holds. Given any finitely\nsupported function assigning rational coefficients to triples\nof non-negative exponents, if the weighted sum of powers of\nthe three volumes vanishes, the function is identically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L454-L454","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","kind":"class","line":437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L437-L465","doc":"**Conjecture (Algebraic independence of QOU hyperbolic volumes).**\n\nThe three hyperbolic volumes Vol(4₁), Vol(5₂), Vol(𝓑₃) are\nalgebraically independent over ℚ.  Equivalently, for any finitely\nsupported function `f : ℕ × ℕ × ℕ → ℚ`, if the sum\n`Σ f(i,j,k) · Vol(4₁)^i · Vol(5₂)^j · Vol(𝓑₃)^k = 0`\nthen `f = 0`.\n\nSince the ground ring ℚ[q, q⁻¹] is a polynomial ring over ℚ,\nalgebraic independence over ℚ implies algebraic independence\nover ℚ[q, q⁻¹] (the volumes are real constants, independent of q).\n\nNote: we use non-negative exponents (ℕ) since the volumes are\nnon-zero reals — any Laurent-style relation `v^{-k}` can be\ncleared by multiplying through by `v^k`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence","label":"conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hyperbolic-volume-transcendence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.infinitely_many_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.infinitely_many_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L414-L420","doc":"Given faithfulness and a non-collapsing tower, infinitely many\nlevel contributions are non-zero.  (Proved from the structure.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.faithful","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L410-L410","doc":"**Faithfulness**: non-trivial obstruction implies non-zero\nvolume contribution at that level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.tower_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.tower_eq","kind":"theorem","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L407-L407","doc":"The towers agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.vtd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.vtd","kind":"def","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L405-L405","doc":"A tower decomposition of some knot volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.ylc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.ylc","kind":"def","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L403-L403","doc":"The lifting condition with obstruction classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful.mk","kind":"ctor","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L401-L401","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CSEvaluationFaithful","kind":"structure","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L396-L412","doc":"**CS evaluation faithfulness.**\nIf the Yekutieli obstruction class κ_n is non-trivial, then\nthe Chern–Simons period integral at level n is non-zero.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:cs-evaluation-faithfulness}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:cs-evaluation-faithfulness","label":"prop:cs-evaluation-faithfulness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/cs-evaluation-faithfulness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volumeTowerDecomp_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volumeTowerDecomp_B3","kind":"def","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L383-L388","doc":"Tower decomposition for Vol(𝓑₃). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volumeTowerDecomp_5_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volumeTowerDecomp_5_2","kind":"def","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L376-L381","doc":"Tower decomposition for Vol(5₂). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volumeTowerDecomp_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volumeTowerDecomp_4_1","kind":"def","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L369-L374","doc":"Tower decomposition for Vol(4₁). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.baselineDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.baselineDecomposition","kind":"def","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L336-L367","doc":"Baseline tower decomposition: all volume concentrated at level 0.\n\nThis is the trivial decomposition Φ₀(K) = Vol(K), Φ_n(K) = 0 for n ≥ 1.\nIt always exists; the non-trivial content is that the obstruction tower\nprovides a REFINEMENT with infinitely many nonzero levels (see\n`CSEvaluationFaithful`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eventually_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eventually_small","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L324-L334","doc":"For any ε > 0, eventually |Φ_n(K)| < ε. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L317-L322","doc":"The level contributions tend to zero.\nProved: summable ⟹ terms → 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.baseline_dominant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.baseline_dominant","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L315-L315","doc":"Classical limit: at level 0, the baseline holonomy gives\nthe dominant contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L312-L312","doc":"The sum recovers the total volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.summable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.summable","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L310-L310","doc":"The series converges absolutely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.levelContribution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.levelContribution","kind":"def","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L308-L308","doc":"Level-n contribution Φ_n(K) from the n-th twisted sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.totalVolume_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.totalVolume_pos","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L306-L306","doc":"The total volume is positive (hyperbolic knot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.totalVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.totalVolume","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L304-L304","doc":"The knot volume being decomposed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.tower","kind":"def","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L302-L302","doc":"The brane tower providing the cosimplicial structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L300-L300","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L295-L315","doc":"**Tower-level volume decomposition.**\nThe hyperbolic volume of a knot K decomposes as a convergent sum\nof Chern–Simons period integrals, one per tower level.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:volume-tower-decomposition}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:volume-tower-decomposition","label":"prop:volume-tower-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/volume-tower-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pairwise_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pairwise_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L284-L287","doc":"All three QOU hyperbolic volumes are pairwise distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2_ne_vol_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2_ne_vol_B3","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L277-L282","doc":"Vol(5₂) ≠ Vol(𝓑₃).  Proof: 5₂ ≈ 2.828 < 7.32 < 8·G = vol_B3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_ne_vol_5_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_ne_vol_5_2","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L272-L275","doc":"Vol(4₁) ≠ Vol(5₂). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_ne_vol_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_ne_vol_B3","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L265-L270","doc":"Vol(4₁) ≠ Vol(𝓑₃).  Proof: 4₁ ≈ 2.030 < 7.32 < 8·G = vol_B3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L254-L255","doc":"Vol(𝓑₃) ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L251-L252","doc":"Vol(5₂) ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L248-L249","doc":"Vol(4₁) ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L239-L244","doc":"Vol(𝓑₃) > 0.  Proof: `vol_B3 = 8 · catalan_G` and `catalan_G > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2_pos","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L233-L237","doc":"Vol(5₂) > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1_pos","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L227-L231","doc":"Vol(4₁) > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L206-L223","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean rings 𝓑₃ (nucleon).\n\n**Exact**: `Vol(𝓑₃) = 8 · G` where `G` is Catalan's constant\n(Adams 1985, octahedral decomposition into 2 regular ideal\noctahedra, each of volume `8 · Λ(π/4) = 4 · G`).\n\nNumerically: 8 · 0.915965594177219… = 7.327724753417752120…\n(i.e. agrees with the SnapPy census measurement\n7.32772475341775 ± 1×10⁻¹⁴ to 14 dps).\n\nDefined as the *symbolic* product `8 · catalan_G` — this means\n`vol_B3 = 8 · catalan_G` is a `rfl` theorem and the previous\n`axiom vol_B3_eq_8_catalan` is discharged.\n\n-- Ref: [adams1985hyperbolic] Adams, C. C. (1985), \"The noncompact hyperbolic\n        3-manifold of minimum volume\", Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 100,\n        601-606. DOI: 10.2307/2045438. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_5_2","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L177-L204","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the three-twist knot 5₂ (strange quark\nper `computations/substrate/knot-volumes.witness.json`\n— NOT the down quark, which is an unknot with negative crossing\norientation per `QOU.Archimedean.DownQuark`).\n\nNumerical: `2.82812208833078` (15 dps, from\n`computations/hyperbolic-volumes.witness.json`\nfield `vol_5_2_decimal_15`, cross-checked against\n`QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity` which uses the identical value).\n\n**Precision upgrade 2026-06-12**: witness now carries 50 dps from\nSnapPy ManifoldHP 3.3.2 (`vol_5_2_decimal_50`); the former AHW-1991\n15-dps anchor `2.82812208833410` had a digit-13–15 transcription\nerror.\n\n**Drift fix 2026-06-08**: previous literal `2.82812208832975`\ndiffered from the witness at digits 11+ (4.35e-12 absolute drift).\nBumped to match the witness — both files now agree.\n\n**Particle attribution fix 2026-06-08 (Copilot PR #1981)**:\nprevious docstring labeled 5₂ as \"down quark\", which conflated it\nwith the unknot-negative-crossing realisation of the down quark.\nThe strange quark is the correct attribution for 5₂ per the\nknot-volumes witness.\n\nPending: add threeTwistEntry to KnotRegistry and extract from\nthere for full provenance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vol_4_1","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L164-L175","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the figure-eight knot 4₁ (Higgs boson).\nExact: 2 · Cl₂(π/3) = 6 · Λ(π/3) ≈ 2.029883212819307250042405\n(two regular ideal tetrahedra, each of volume Cl₂(π/3) = 3Λ(π/3)).\n\nCorrected 2026-08-09: this docstring and the §1 summary above both\nread `3 · Cl₂(π/3)`, which is 3.0448…, not the 2.0298… literal the\ndefinition actually carries. The same slip is live in four other\ndocstrings — `QOU/MassDerivation.lean`, `QOU/HadronicMass.lean`,\n`observations/local-substrate-q.lean`,\n`observations/skein-mass-relation.lean` — while the rest of the\ncorpus has `2 · Cl₂(π/3)` correctly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.catalan_G_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.catalan_G_pos","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L145-L148","doc":"Catalan's constant is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.catalan_G_numerical_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.catalan_G_numerical_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L80-L143","doc":"Numerical bounds on Catalan's constant: `0.915 < G < 0.916`.\n\n**Theorem** (was an axiom until 2026-06-10; discharged via the\nalternating-series partial-sum bracket — queue item\n`lean-catalan-G-numerical-bound`).\n\nMethod: `G = Σ (-1)^k·f k` with `f k = 1/(2k+1)²` antitone → 0, so\neven partial sums bound `G` from below and odd ones from above\n(`Antitone.alternating_series_le_tendsto` /\n`Antitone.tendsto_le_alternating_series`).  The margins force the\ntruncation orders: `0.916 − G ≈ 3.44e-5`, so the upper bracket\nneeds the odd sum `S₉₃` (error ≤ 1/187² ≈ 2.86e-5); the lower needs\nonly `S₂₀` (error ≤ 1/41² ≈ 5.9e-4 against a 9.66e-4 margin).\nExact rational pre-check: `S₂₀ = 0.91565…`, `S₉₃ = 0.91598…`.\n\nLiterature value (mpmath `mp.catalan` at 50 dps, OEIS A006752):\n`G ≈ 0.915965594177219015054603514…`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.catalan_G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.catalan_G","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean#L64-L77","doc":"Catalan's constant `G = Σ_{k=0}^∞ (-1)^k / (2k+1)²`.\n\nOEIS A006752, 24-digit value 0.915965594177219015054603514…\n\nStandard reference: [lewin1981] Lewin, \"Polylogarithms and Associated\nFunctions\", North-Holland, eq. 1.7.8.\n\nNot yet in Mathlib (verified via `lean_loogle`, `lean_leansearch`\nqueries on 2026-05-25); introduced here as a noncomputable def\npending upstream contribution. ","signatureChunk":0}]}